ronchopulmonary dysplasia develops.</article-title><source>Pediatrics</source><year>1996</year><volume>97</volume><fpage>210</fpage><lpage>215</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8584379</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yoon</surname><given-names>BH</given-names></name><name><surname>Romero</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Jun</surname><given-names>JK</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>KH</given-names></name><name><surname>Park</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Ghezzi</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>BI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Amniotic fluid cytokines (interleukin-6, tumor necrosis factor-alpha, interleukin-1 beta, and interleukin-8) and the risk for the development of bronchopulmonary dysplasia.</article-title><source>Am J Obstet Gynecol</source><year>1997</year><volume>177</volume><fpage>825</fpage><lpage>830</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9369827</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0002-9378(97)70276-X</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fung</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Bawden</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Chow</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chorioamnionitis and outcome in extremely preterm infants.</article-title><source>Ann Acad Med Singapore</source><year>2003</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>305</fpage><lpage>310</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12854373</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>D'Alquen</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Kramer</surname><given-names>BW</given-names></name><name><surname>Seidenspinner</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Marx</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Berg</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Groneck</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Speer</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Activation of umbilical cord endothelial cells and fetal inflammatory response in preterm infants with chorioamnionitis and funisitis.</article-title><source>Pediatr Res</source><year>2005</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>263</fpage><lpage>269</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15611353</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1203/01.PDR.0000148713.48218.86</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zhang</surname><given-names>S-X</given-names></name></person-group><source>An Atlas of Histology</source><year>1999</year><publisher-name>New York, NY: Springer</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Clapp</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The use of umbilical cord blood as a cellular source for correction of genetic diseases affecting the hematopoietic system.</article-title><source>Stem Cells</source><year>1995</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>613</fpage><lpage>621</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8590863</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vizza</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Correr</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Goranova</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Heyn</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Angelucci</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><name><surname>Forleo</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Motta</surname><given-names>PM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The collagen skeleton of the human umbilical cord at term. A scanning electron microscopy study after 2N-NaOH maceration.</article-title><source>ReprodFertil Dev</source><year>1996</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>885</fpage><lpage>894</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="other"><article-title>Extremely Low Gestational Age Newborns (ELGAN): a study of babies born too soon</article-title><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.elganstudy.org/"/></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Benjamini</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Hochberg</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Controlling the false discoveryrate: a new and powerful approach to multiple testing.</article-title><source>J RoyStat Soc Ser B</source><year>1995</year><volume>57</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>300</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mootha</surname><given-names>VK</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindgren</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Eriksson</surname><given-names>KF</given-names></name><name><surname>Subramanian</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Sihag</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Lehar</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Puigserver</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Carlsson</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Ridderstrale</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Laurila</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-